  "title": "The Mongol conquests",
  "summary": "From 1206 Genghis Khan and his successors conquered almost all of Asia, from the Black Sea to Korea, with fast cavalry, diplomacy and terror, creating the largest contiguous land empire in world history. Cities were destroyed down to their foundations, civilians massacred and irrigation systems wrecked; Baghdad was sacked in 1258. The Mongols also linked East and West through expanded trade routes, embassies and travellers. The empire split into four khanates, and the Yuan dynasty in China lasted until 1368.",
